# Rewrites for statichost.eu (also understood by Netlify and Cloudflare Pages).
# The page asks for /api/weather on its own address (with latitude, longitude... for Warsaw, from live-config.js); the host forwards it to
# Open-Meteo and returns the answer, so visitors never contact Open-Meteo themselves.
# NOTE: statichost forwards only the query string the browser sends. A query written into the destination here is IGNORED (tried: the
# answer came back empty), so the location cannot be pinned in this file.
/api/weather  https://api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast  200

# The CV is a page at /cv/ (src/pages/cv.astro), with the PDF linked from it. The old address /resume/ is sent on to it.
/resume/  /cv/  301

# The CV as a file. /cv.pdf is the permanent address everything links to; the line below is THE ONE PLACE that says which file in public/ it is.
# When you replace the CV: put the new PDF in public/, change its name here, and delete the old one. (The build fails if the file is missing.)
/cv.pdf   /lukasz-wojcik-cv-11-2026.pdf  200

# The GPG public key. /gpg is the permanent address (Contact page, llms.txt); the line below says which file in public/ it is.
/gpg      /assets/lukasz_wojcik_gpg.asc  200
/gpg/     /assets/lukasz_wojcik_gpg.asc  200
